      "question": "Based on the FY2024 filings, compare the primary strategic objectives of AEP and ED.",
      "expected_answer": "AEP's filing does not explicitly state a strategic objective in the provided excerpts; it lists risk factors. ED's filing states: 'Con Edison seeks to provide shareholder value through continued dividend growth, supported by earnings growth in regulated utilities and electric transmission projects.' Thus, ED has a clear shareholder-focused strategy, while AEP's excerpt concentrates on forward-looking statements and risks.",
      "predicted_answer": "**Conclusion:** ED explicitly states a primary strategic objective focused on shareholder value through dividend growth supported by regulated utility earnings and transmission investments, while the supplied AEP Item 7 excerpts do not contain an explicitly stated primary strategic objective.\n\n- **AEP FY2024:** The retrieved Item 7 excerpts consist of forward-looking statement disclaimers, risk factors, and incorporation-by-reference notices. No explicit statement of primary strategic objectives is present in the supplied evidence [E1][E3].\n\n- **ED FY2024:** Con Edison explicitly seeks \"to provide shareholder value through continued dividend growth, supported by earnings growth in regulated utilities and electric transmission projects\" [E2]. The company also acknowledges strategic risks from the external environment, including the energy transition (distributed energy resources, electrification, and climate policy impacts on gas/steam demand).\n\n**Comparison:** ED's disclosed Item 7 clearly frames shareholder value creation as its primary objective, whereas the supplied AEP Item 7 excerpts do not contain a comparable explicit strategic objective statement—only risk disclosures and procedural references.\n\nSources:\n[E1] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E2] ED_2024.html — Item 7. The Companies’ Strategies May Not Be Effective To Address Changes In The External Business Environment\n[E3] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS",
